The public-domain dedication in UNLICENSE applies only to this component's
original code, original/generated artwork, and original texture layouts. It does
not apply to the referenced Minecraft apple outline or the third-party netherite
horse armor assets described below.

Original item artwork was developed using OpenAI ImageGen. Horseshoes and saddles
were cleaned up on a native 16x16 pixel grid; tools/build-item-textures.ps1 records
and regenerates their final pixels. The horse effigy reuses the wooden chess
knight created for this project. Prompts are recorded in art-prompts.json.
tools/build-entity-textures.ps1 regenerates the original hoof and empty-slot textures.
The three appearance apple concepts were created with built-in OpenAI ImageGen;
tools/apple-prompts.json records the original prompts; tools/apple-prompts-v2.json
records the shared-shape revision; tools/skeleton-apple-prompt-v5.json records the
32x32 skeleton revision with dark contours and the vanilla stem. tools/build-apple-textures.ps1 and
tools/build-skeleton-apple.ps1 record the final pixels at their native resolutions.
The apple contour and stalk follow Minecraft Java 1.21.1's
apple texture, which remains Mojang's property. The skeleton apple's open ribs
take visual inspiration from mongoose_artist's Born in Chaos Bone Heart; none of
that item's pixels are included. Reference details are in tools/apple-style-revision.md.
The cosmetic horse appearances reference
Minecraft's zombie/skeleton horse textures at runtime without bundling those assets.
The inventory icon edit prompt and native-grid cleanup are recorded in tools/interface-icons.md.

Minecraft, NeoForge, and their models, APIs, and runtime resources remain the
property of their respective authors. The renderer references Minecraft's horse
models and GUI resources at runtime; those models are not bundled here.

